# VOX — sample environment. Names only, never real values: the keys live in ~/.config/, outside
# the repo. `make setup` copies this file to .env if you do not have one.
#
# Every tunable below is commented out on purpose. src/config.py holds the defaults, and an
# uncommented copy here would silently override a default that later changes — so uncomment a line
# only when you mean to change it. The value shown after `=` is the current default.
#
# The exception is credentials: they have no default, and a MISSING one deliberately does not fall
# back to a local arm. That is a config bug, and hiding it behind a worse transcript is worse than
# stopping. See the fallback section of ARCHITECTURE.md.

# --- credentials -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
HF_TOKEN=
# only needed for gated repos; the pinned tokenizer mirror needs none
GROQ_API_KEY=
# STT default + the gpt-oss LLM arm            free tier: https://console.groq.com
NVIDIA_API_KEY=
# LLM default (Llama-3.1-8B)                   free tier: https://build.nvidia.com

# --- arm selection: an alias, an HF repo id, or repo/id@provider. A CLI flag beats the env -----
# VOX_STT_MODEL=openai/whisper-large-v3-turbo         (alias: turbo)
# VOX_LLM_MODEL=meta-llama/Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct      (alias: llama-8b)
# VOX_TTS_MODEL=hexgrad/Kokoro-82M                    (alias: kokoro)
# VOX_EMBED_MODEL=BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5              (alias: bge-small)

# --- session and audio -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VOX_SESSION_MINUTES=3           how long `make demo` listens
# VOX_SESSION_QUIET_LIMIT=2       consecutive silent listens before the session ends itself
# VOX_TTS_VOICE=af_heart          Kokoro voice
# VOX_STT_LANGUAGE=en
# VOX_STT_BIAS=0                  1 enables Whisper vocabulary biasing via initial_prompt (VOX-021)

# --- timeouts ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VOX_REMOTE_TIMEOUT_S=10         a hosted arm's budget before the turn falls back to its local arm
# VOX_LOCAL_TIMEOUT_S=120
# VOX_OLLAMA_HOST=http://localhost:11434   where the local LLM fallback runs. No key — the weights
#                                          are on this machine and nobody is billed

# --- knowledge base: chunking. Re-run `make index` after changing any of these ------------------
# VOX_SOURCES_DIR=./sources
# VOX_CHUNKS_FILE=./runs/chunks.jsonl
# VOX_EMBEDDINGS_FILE=./runs/embeddings.npz
# VOX_CHUNK_TOKENS=300
# VOX_CHUNK_OVERLAP_TOKENS=50
# VOX_TOKENIZER_REPO=NousResearch/Meta-Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct   a mirror of the gated 3.1 tokenizer
# VOX_EMBED_BATCH=16

# --- retrieval: the two measured floors and the fusion. Re-run `make floors` if you touch them --
# VOX_HYBRID_RETRIEVAL=1          0 = BM25 only, i.e. VOX-030's behaviour
# VOX_RETRIEVAL_TOP_K=5           k=5 is ~5.1x the plain prompt; the knob that moves first
# VOX_RETRIEVAL_SCORE_FLOOR=0.28  calibrated on evals/dev: answerable min 0.320 vs absent max 0.234
# VOX_DENSE_SCORE_FLOOR=0.65      chosen, NOT derived — the dense column does not separate
# VOX_RRF_K=60
# VOX_FUSION_CANDIDATES=20
# VOX_BM25_K1=1.5
# VOX_BM25_B=0.75
# VOX_BM25_EPSILON=0.25

# --- the grounded answer -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# VOX_ANSWER_MAX_TOKENS=500       the answer stage's own ceiling. nlu.MAX_TOKENS (120) is a spoken
#                                 reply's guardrail and cut three live answers off mid-sentence

# VAD and barge-in thresholds are NOT here — they live in config.yaml (VOX-012), because
# scripts/tune_vad.py measures their effect on the dev set and a measured knob belongs next to
# the note about what it was measured against.
